    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this May 30th slate, **Josh Naylor** (64.20) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.48) anchor the core, benefiting significantly from matchups against Ryne Nelson and Kumar Rocker, respectively. **Naylor** is the standout play today; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA and a premier spot in the heart of the order provides the highest floor for RBI production. **James Wood** (62.98) also warrants high confidence. While his score is slightly tempered by a difficult matchup against Michael King, his elite 40% stolen base expectation in our specific weighting model makes him an essential start, as he remains our primary weapon for closing the gap in the scarcest category. **Brice Turang** (60.94) and **Corbin Carroll** (59.57) round out the high-upside group, with **Carroll** specifically gaining significant equity from his #2 spot in the order, effectively mitigating the threat posed by Bryan Woo.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Austin Riley**, who carries a solid base projection but was ultimately benched due to his absence from the starting lineup. Had he been active, his high SB-weighted hold percentage would have easily slotted him into the UTIL or 1B spot over our current options. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Gabriel Moreno** (46.15) and **Cole Young** (43.47), both of whom face high-skill pitchers that suppress their raw projections. **Travis Bazzana** (46.58) remains in the lineup purely as a volume play; while his SP_xERA matchup against Sonny Gray is daunting, his leadoff placement grants him the necessary plate appearances to potentially impact the R and SB columns. We are monitoring all lineups closely for any late-breaking weather patterns or fatigue-related scratches, as our bench depth is currently depleted by the IL stints of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story**. We remain ready to pivot to any available high-speed depth, such as **Zach McKinstry** or **Henry Bolte**, should our current starters see their playing time unexpectedly capped.",
